  "limitations": [
    "New native production message-pipe owner is exercised through Win32 API mocks on Linux, including a real transaction machine calling that owner with explicitly synthetic authorization. This is not an actual Windows pipe, peer-authentication or adversarial OS acceptance test.",
    "Raw owner intentionally does not implement trusted ServerTransport/ClientTransport. Last-read-message token authorization/restoration, actual connected-server validation, host/CLI/GUI public transport integration remain required.",
    "New SDK assertions/signatures and production native_link function-address retention were edited but not compiled or executed natively. Prior Windows automatic approval quota rejection was not retried or bypassed. Linux pointer-width layout test and existing Linux/X11 ABI checks do not prove Windows SDK/ABI or x86 build correctness.",
    "close/disconnect never wait; owners require repeated bounded cleanup polls within an outer absolute deadline. Drop makes one nonblocking fallback and may deliberately retain pending memory/handles until process exit. Returned factory cleanup is a snapshot before any later Drop fallback, not a proof later cleanup succeeded.",
